# TUXEDO Pulse 14 Gen4 function row
# Fn+F3 is emitted by the TUXEDO driver as a synthetic Super+Alt+F6 chord
# (keycode 72) on its virtual input device -- see report_gauge_key_combo() in
# tuxedo_nb05_keyboard.c.
#
# Two gotchas, both verified with wev:
#   --release leaves the press unclaimed, so the chord falls through to the
#   focused window (Emacs: "M-s-<F6> is undefined").
#   --input-device matches on release but NOT on press, so a device-scoped
#   press binding silently never fires. Hence plain bindcode on the press.
# Bare Super/Alt still reach clients; harmless, nothing looks them up alone.
bindcode Mod4+Mod1+72 exec laptop-key profile
bindsym XF86Display exec laptop-key display
